	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Usage

Browse your Rex workspaces via the `ws` keyword.

- &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open the workspace, building its session first if it isn't running
- &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Edit workspaces.lua
- &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Rebuild the workspace from its definition

Workspaces are defined in your Rex configuration, in the `rexws_open` and `rexws_list` actions this workflow calls. The first time you use the keyword, it offers to set them up for you.

Workspaces can also be opened from a script using the `open` external trigger, passing the workspace's name.
</string>
